# ~/.zprofile -- login shells only, sourced AFTER /etc/zprofile and BEFORE .zshrc.
#
# This file exists to undo one specific thing macOS does. /etc/zprofile runs
# path_helper, which rebuilds PATH with the system directories first and appends
# everything else to the end. That silently demotes the entries .zshenv put at
# the front: in a login shell ~/.bin lands *below* /usr/bin and /opt/homebrew/bin,
# so a script there can never shadow a system or Homebrew command -- which is the
# entire reason the directory exists.
#
# Re-prepending the same array restores the intended order. `typeset -U path`
# from .zshenv makes this a move rather than a duplicate.
#
# macOS only; chezmoi skips this file on other platforms (see .chezmoiignore).
path=($my_path $path)
